---
description: Keep remote Git history intact when publishing changes
alwaysApply: true
---

# Safe Git publishing

- Never run a forced push: `git push --force`, `git push --force-with-lease`,
  `git push -f`, or an equivalent forced refspec (such as `+branch`).
- If a normal push is rejected, fetch the remote state, inspect the divergence,
  resolve it locally with a merge or rebase as appropriate, run the affected
  checks, then retry a normal push.
- If preserving both histories cannot be resolved safely, stop and ask for
  direction. Do not overwrite remote commits to unblock delivery.
